on, and whether that symmetry means the two should be treated as linked.\n\nI'm working out the threshold where passing beats submitting: pass wins when (1-ρ)(2-q) < 2ρ, so with q=0.5 the cutoff is ρ > 3/7. Since the twins are identical and reason symmetrically, I'm treating ρ as high, which points to passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9742,"completion_tokens":783,"total_tokens":10525,"cost":0.054628,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.054628,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038968,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01566},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":425,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}